  "answer": "No. The Aussie dollar is strong against the yen right now, though it has slipped a little from its recent peak.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought ¥109.67 on 16 October 2026.\n- **One year ago:** it bought ¥100.84 at the end of October 2025. That makes it about 9% higher over the year.\n- **Start of 2025:** it bought ¥96.14 in January 2025, and ¥91.43 in April 2025, the low of this dataset (which starts in January 2025). The latest rate is about 14% above January 2025 and about 20% above that April low.\n- **Recent peak:** it reached about ¥114.3 at the end of April 2026 and ¥114.5 at the end of August 2026.\n- **Past six weeks:** it has fallen about 4%, from ¥114.63 on 1 September to about ¥110 in October. Since mid-September it has stayed in a narrow range of roughly ¥109.4 to ¥112.\n\nThe AUD is weaker than it was in the spring and summer, but it is well above its 2025 levels. The yen has been the weaker currency over this period.",
